{"id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-1-hessian-center","title":"lem:dc-ch3-4-1-hessian-center","path":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods.md","line":922,"body":"","kind":"lemma","status":"not_started","tex":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods.tex#lem:dc-ch3-4-1-hessian-center","uses":["[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-1-ddF]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-1-radialcoord]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods.tex","label":"lem:dc-ch3-4-1-hessian-center","line":2599,"source":"\\begin{lemma}[center Hessian: $\\partial^2 F/\\partial t^2(0,p,v)=2|v|^2$]\n  \\label{lem:dc-ch3-4-1-hessian-center}\n\n  \\uses{lem:dc-ch3-4-1-ddF, lem:dc-ch3-4-1-radialcoord}\n\n  \\dcref{ch3:4.1}\n  For $q=p$ the geodesic through $p$ with velocity $v$ is the radial ray, so\n  $u(t)=tv$ (\\cref{lem:dc-ch3-4-1-radialcoord}), $u'=v$, $u''=0$, and by\n  \\cref{lem:dc-ch3-4-1-ddF}\n  $$\\frac{\\partial^2 F}{\\partial t^2}(0,p,v)=2|v|_p^2.$$\n  In particular for a unit $v$ this equals $2>0$, the strict-minimum seed.\n\\end{lemma}\n\\begin{proof}\n  \\sketch\n\n  With $u(t)=tv$ the first-derivative field is\n  $s\\mapsto 2\\langle v,sv\\rangle_p=2s\\,|v|_p^2$, whose derivative at $0$ is\n  $2|v|_p^2$.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Lemma</div></section>[center Hessian: <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\partial ^2 F/\\partial t^2(0,p,v)=2|v|^2$\">$\\partial ^2 F/\\partial t^2(0,p,v)=2|v|^2$</span>] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6c656d3a64632d6368332d342d312d6865737369616e2d63656e746572\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-4-1-ddF\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-4-1-ddF</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-4-1-radialcoord\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-4-1-radialcoord</a> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source-references\" role=\"list\" style=\"display:block\"><span class=\"tex-dcref\" role=\"listitem\" style=\"display:block\">1. ch3:4.1</span></span>For <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$q=p$\">$q=p$</span> the geodesic through <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$p$\">$p$</span> with velocity <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$v$\">$v$</span> is the radial ray, so <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$u(t)=tv$\">$u(t)=tv$</span> (<a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-4-1-radialcoord\" data-tex-node=\"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-1-radialcoord\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6c656d3a64632d6368332d342d312d72616469616c636f6f7264\">section 3</a>), <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$u&#x27;=v$\">$u&#x27;=v$</span>, <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$u&#x27;&#x27;=0$\">$u&#x27;&#x27;=0$</span>, and by <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-4-1-ddF\" data-tex-node=\"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-1-ddF\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6c656d3a64632d6368332d342d312d646446\">section 3</a> <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[ \\frac{\\partial ^2 F}{\\partial t^2}(0,p,v)=2|v|_p^2. \\]\">\\[ \\frac{\\partial ^2 F}{\\partial t^2}(0,p,v)=2|v|_p^2. \\]</span> In particular for a unit <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$v$\">$v$</span> this equals <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$2&gt;0$\">$2&gt;0$</span>, the strict-minimum seed.  <section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p>\\sketch </p><p>With <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$u(t)=tv$\">$u(t)=tv$</span> the first-derivative field is <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$s\\mapsto 2\\langle v,sv\\rangle _p=2s\\, |v|_p^2$\">$s\\mapsto 2\\langle v,sv\\rangle _p=2s\\, |v|_p^2$</span>, whose derivative at <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$0$\">$0$</span> is <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$2|v|_p^2$\">$2|v|_p^2$</span>. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-1-radialcoord","next":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-1-posdef","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-1-ddF","title":"lem:dc-ch3-4-1-ddF","label":"lem:dc-ch3-4-1-ddF"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-1-radialcoord","title":"lem:dc-ch3-4-1-radialcoord","label":"lem:dc-ch3-4-1-radialcoord"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-1","title":"lem:dc-ch3-4-1","label":"lem:dc-ch3-4-1"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-1-hessian-center","title":"lem:dc-ch3-4-1-hessian-center","tex":"\\begin{lemma}[center Hessian: $\\partial^2 F/\\partial t^2(0,p,v)=2|v|^2$]\n  \\label{lem:dc-ch3-4-1-hessian-center}\n\n  \\uses{lem:dc-ch3-4-1-ddF, lem:dc-ch3-4-1-radialcoord}\n\n  \\dcref{ch3:4.1}\n  For $q=p$ the geodesic through $p$ with velocity $v$ is the radial ray, so\n  $u(t)=tv$ (\\cref{lem:dc-ch3-4-1-radialcoord}), $u'=v$, $u''=0$, and by\n  \\cref{lem:dc-ch3-4-1-ddF}\n  $$\\frac{\\partial^2 F}{\\partial t^2}(0,p,v)=2|v|_p^2.$$\n  In particular for a unit $v$ this equals $2>0$, the strict-minimum seed.\n\\end{lemma}\n\\begin{proof}\n  \\sketch\n\n  With $u(t)=tv$ the first-derivative field is\n  $s\\mapsto 2\\langle v,sv\\rangle_p=2s\\,|v|_p^2$, whose derivative at $0$ is\n  $2|v|_p^2$.\n\\end{proof}","source":"tex/references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-1-ddF","title":"lem:dc-ch3-4-1-ddF","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-1-radialcoord","title":"lem:dc-ch3-4-1-radialcoord","description":""}],"dependencies_omitted":0,"unresolved_dependencies":[],"unresolved_omitted":0}}